{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789885738332,"sessionID":"ses_f428ff92affeQ6wiY0s4pQPZG0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_923910f1faf54d35ac502395","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"& \"C:\\xampp\\php\\php.exe\" \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\ias2build\\extract_long.php\""},"output":"### ch1-q11 (gap=42 lens=[55,101,59,70] ca=1)\nQ: At the exit interview, management agrees to assign an owner and a deadline for applying the security patches the audit recommended. Which exit interview purpose does this reflect?\n  [0] Clarifying the evidence behind the audit's conclusions.\n  [CORRECT*] Discussing improvements such as recommendations, corrective actions, responsibilities, and timelines.\n  [2] Obtaining the auditor's response to management's questions.\n  [3] Preparing the approval timeline for the signature of the final report.\n\n### ch1-q08 (gap=40 lens=[60,55,57,97] ca=3)\nQ: The audit client invites a staff member who directly operated the audited systems to attend the exit interview. As one of the other participants, this person is expected to...\n  [0] Choose which findings will appear in the final audit report.\n  [1] Moderate the meeting and keep both sides on the agenda.\n  [2] Draft the corrective action plan before the meeting ends.\n  [CORRECT*] Provide relevant information, clarification, or perspective on the audited processes or findings.\n\n### ch1-q30 (gap=31 lens=[67,67,98,53] ca=2)\nQ: A stakeholder asks why the audit team holds a formal presentation of findings after the report is finalized. Which reason from the lesson supports holding it?\n  [0] To replace the written report with an oral summary of the findings.\n  [1] To revise the audit conclusions after hearing stakeholder feedback.\n  [CORRECT*] To provide a shared moment for understanding results and moving forward with clear accountability.\n  [3] To record who attended so the audit file is complete.\n\n### ch1-q19 (gap=30 lens=[62,59,92,70] ca=2)\nQ: According to the lesson, data analysis in auditing is best described as...\n  [0] The storage of finished audit reports in a central repository.\n  [1] A schedule that tracks the progress of the audit fieldwork.\n  [CORRECT*] The intelligence generated from reviewing audit-related information, often using technology.\n  [3] A meeting format used when witnesses disagree with the audit findings.\n\n### ch1-q12 (gap=29 lens=[72,64,64,93] ca=3)\nQ: During the exit interview, the auditor finds that the IT department has not submitted its latest access-control review or user-permission logs. Which two questions does the auditor ask about this missing information?\n  [0] Which tool generated the logs, and what format should they be stored in?\n  [1] How long must the logs be kept, and who owns the storage server?\n  [2] Why was the review skipped, and can it be repeated next quarter?\n  [CORRECT*] Who is responsible for providing the missing information, and when can the auditor expect it?\n\n### ch4-q01 (gap=27 lens=[80,59,53,53] ca=0)\nQ: In the reviewer, risk identification is best described as the process of what?\n  [CORRECT*] finding, recognizing, and documenting potential risks that may affect a project.\n  [1] calculating the exact dollar loss for each possible threat.\n  [2] removing the threats that could cause project delays.\n  [3] assigning an owner to every risk on the project list.\n\n### ch1-q15 (gap=26 lens=[60,91,65,65] ca=1)\nQ: Compare closing an audit with an exit interview against publishing straight away. What does the lesson say the exit interview specifically prevents?\n  [0] Delays, because the meeting shortens the fieldwork schedule.\n  [CORRECT*] Surprises, because findings and next steps are discussed before the final report is issued.\n  [2] Errors, because the report is fully rewritten during the meeting.\n  [3] Costs, because the meeting removes the need for a written report.\n\n### ch1-q22 (gap=23 lens=[60,56,80,57] ca=2)\nQ: Before analyzing collected data, the auditor cleans it for use. Which task belongs to this data wrangling stage?\n  [0] Choosing which charts will appear in the final presentation.\n  [1] Writing the recommendations section of the audit report.\n  [CORRECT*] Searching for outliers, handling null values, and checking for incorrect inputs.\n  [3] Deciding which questions the analysis will try to answer.\n\n### ch1-q27 (gap=22 lens=[93,68,72,71] ca=0)\nQ: According to the lesson, which of the following is one of the purposes of an audit report?\n  [CORRECT*] Formal communication, documentation of evidence, and initiation of corrective action closure.\n  [1] Staff training, system rollout, and patch scheduling for the entity.\n  [2] Budget forecasting, revenue projection, and cost control for the entity.\n  [3] Vendor selection, contract negotiation, and hiring for the next period.\n\n### ch1-q17 (gap=21 lens=[43,58,49,70] ca=3)\nQ: After the exit interview, a disagreement between the auditor and the audited entity remains unresolved. The entity asks to have the point removed from the report. What does the lesson say the auditors should do?\n  [0] Restart the audit from the fieldwork phase.\n  [1] Withdraw the finding to preserve the working relationship.\n  [2] Ask a neutral third party to mediate the dispute.\n  [CORRECT*] Document the difference of opinion and include it in the audit report.\n\n### ch2-q20 (gap=21 lens=[55,34,34,29] ca=0)\nQ: In a HIDS, what does File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) primarily do?\n  [CORRECT*] Compares current file states against baseline snapshots\n  [1] Encrypts confidential system files\n  [2] Blocks inbound network connections\n  [3] Stores user login credentials\n\n### ch1-q06 (gap=19 lens=[64,77,58,57] ca=1)\nQ: During the exit interview, which activity does the audit team primarily carry out?\n  [0] Approving the corrective actions chosen by the department heads.\n  [CORRECT*] Presenting and explaining the audit findings and facilitating the discussion.\n  [2] Committing to fix every deficiency found during the audit.\n  [3] Signing the final report on behalf of the audited entity.\n\n### ch1-q02 (gap=18 lens=[98,83,70,80] ca=0)\nQ: After an audit, a division uses the findings to strengthen its firewall rules and update its incident-response plan. Which option best reflects the core purpose of post-audit activities in this example?\n  [CORRECT*] To help the organization understand the findings, address the issues found, and plan improvements.\n  [1] To decide whether the auditors completed the engagement within its approved budget.\n  [2] To determine which systems will be excluded from the next audit cycle.\n  [3] To compare the division's controls against published industry benchmark reports.\n\n### ch1-q14 (gap=18 lens=[70,62,87,69] ca=2)\nQ: A manager says the exit interview resolves issues early. Which outcome best shows this advantage in practice?\n  [0] Findings remain confidential until the report is officially published.\n  [1] Minor concerns disappear once the report is sent for printing.\n  [CORRECT*] Misunderstandings and missing information are addressed before the report is finalized.\n  [3] The audited entity revises the findings after the report is released.\n\n### ch2-q17 (gap=17 lens=[38,53,36,30] ca=1)\nQ: How does stateful protocol analysis mainly differ from anomaly-based analysis?\n  [0] It learns normal behavior from history\n  [CORRECT*] It compares activity against vendor protocol profiles\n  [2] It relies on known attack signatures\n  [3] It monitors pre-set thresholds\n\n### ch1-q03 (gap=16 lens=[73,90,77,74] ca=1)\nQ: An exit interview, also called an exit or closing meeting, is held at which point in the audit process?\n  [0] Right after the final audit report is released to the board of directors.\n  [CORRECT*] At the conclusion of audit fieldwork, when necessary, before the final report is released.\n  [2] At the start of fieldwork to confirm the scope and timetable with management.\n  [3] Whenever the financial statements show a suspected case of material fraud.\n\n### ch1-q25 (gap=15 lens=[65,71,80,65] ca=2)\nQ: A supervisor asks which method would best forecast how login volumes will change next quarter. Which choice applies the lesson's methods correctly?\n  [0] Descriptive analysis, since it summarizes the key login sections.\n  [1] Diagnostic analysis, since it searches for the cause of login problems.\n  [CORRECT*] Predictive analysis, since it combines historical data and statistical modeling.\n  [3] Data wrangling, since it cleans the outliers before the forecast.\n\n### ch1-q09 (gap=14 lens=[77,63,63,55] ca=0)\nQ: An attendee believes the auditor judged a control against an outdated policy, but the auditor actually used the current version. Which exit interview objective does the auditor serve by clearing up this confusion?\n  [CORRECT*] Clarify, by resolving the misunderstanding about the evidence or conclusions.\n  [1] Obtain the management response to the proposed recommendations.\n  [2] Discuss improvements and assign responsibilities and timelines.\n  [3] Prepare the draft report for final review and approval.\n\n### ch4-q08 (gap=14 lens=[57,53,53,67] ca=3)\nQ: Which materials are reviewed during documentation review to uncover potential risks?\n  [0] vendor prices, office space, utilities, and rental costs.\n  [1] employee salaries, leaves, and overnight shift plans.\n  [2] client complaints, surveys, and past service records.\n  [CORRECT*] project documents, contracts, schedules, requirements, and reports.\n\n### ch2-q26 (gap=13 lens=[27,26,39,24] ca=2)\nQ: Why do administrators isolate a suspected compromised host instead of immediately shutting it down?\n  [0] To reduce electricity usage\n  [1] To improve processor speed\n  [CORRECT*] To let investigators examine the system\n  [3] To free up network ports\n\n### ch4-q28 (gap=13 lens=[67,63,61,76] ca=3)\nQ: How does the reviewer define monitoring and controlling the risk response?\n  [0] preparing the assessment after the response plan has been executed.\n  [1] documenting the high-severity risks during risk identification.\n  [2] selecting fresh strategies once the budget has been approved.\n  [CORRECT*] tracking identified risks and reviewing the effectiveness of response plans.\n\n### ch1-q01 (gap=12 lens=[94,79,82,84] ca=0)\nQ: Which of the following best defines post-audit activities?\n  [CORRECT*] The activities done after the audit to review, analyze, document, and communicate its results.\n  [1] The steps taken before fieldwork to budget the time and cost of the engagement.\n  [2] The short notices regulators send about upcoming mandatory compliance inspections.\n  [3] The tests executed during fieldwork to verify the accuracy of recorded transactions.\n\n### ch4-q02 (gap=12 lens=[66,78,66,65] ca=1)\nQ: Where in the process does risk identification occur, and what core question does it ask?\n  [0] after assessment, asking how much each risk will cost the project.\n  [CORRECT*] at the starting point, asking what could go wrong while developing the system.\n  [2] at the final step, asking which responses worked in past projects.\n  [3] after monitoring, asking whether the budget still fits the needs.\n\n### ch4-q12 (gap=12 lens=[42,45,54,41] ca=2)\nQ: A startup gives a new vendor a quick Medium rating during a team discussion. What does this show?\n  [0] a statistical test built from vendor data.\n  [1] a dollar-based measure of the potential loss.\n  [CORRECT*] a qualitative judgment-based rating in the discussion.\n  [3] a formal audit of the vendor's past work.\n\nTOTAL flagged (unique-longest, gap>=12): 24\n","metadata":{"output":"### ch1-q11 (gap=42 lens=[55,101,59,70] ca=1)\nQ: At the exit interview, management agrees to assign an owner and a deadline for applying the security patches the audit recommended. Which exit interview purpose does this reflect?\n  [0] Clarifying the evidence behind the audi