{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789885893822,"sessionID":"ses_f428ff92affeQ6wiY0s4pQPZG0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_9ac029d1f9fa49c59b1eed71","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"& \"C:\\xampp\\php\\php.exe\" \"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\ias2build\\extract7.php\""},"output":"### ch1-q10 lens=[72,70,81,67] ca=2\nQ: Management wants to add background on why a server outage delayed a control test during the audit. Which exit interview purpose allows management to provide this explanation?\n  [0] (72) Clarify, so the auditor can verify the evidence used in the conclusions.\n  [1] (70) Discuss improvements, so the team can set corrective action deadlines.\n  [2] (81) CORRECT* Obtain the management response, which allows explanations and additional context.\n  [3] (67) Prepare, so the client can schedule the final report delivery date.\n\n### ch1-q19 lens=[79,77,89,73] ca=2\nQ: According to the lesson, data analysis in auditing is best described as...\n  [0] (79) The organized storage of finished audit reports in a central repository system.\n  [1] (77) A schedule that tracks the progress of the audit fieldwork and its deadlines.\n  [2] (89) CORRECT* The intelligence generated by reviewing audit-related information, often with technology.\n  [3] (73) A meeting format used when witnesses disagree about the audit's findings.\n\n### ch1-q26 lens=[56,52,57,67] ca=3\nQ: In Step 5 (interpret results), the lesson says combining multiple visualizations in one report enables users to...\n  [0] (56) Close the analysis cycle and archive the working papers.\n  [1] (52) Remove findings that leaders consider too technical.\n  [2] (57) Replace the written audit report with a single dashboard.\n  [3] (67) CORRECT* Tell a story leaders can act on, one that prompts deeper questions.\n\n### ch3-q02 lens=[50,49,61,51] ca=2\nQ: Which statement best describes the core concept of the deep-dive exit interview?\n  [0] (50) It is a written record filed after the audit ends.\n  [1] (49) It is a formal memorandum addressed to the board.\n  [2] (61) CORRECT* It is an initial verbal debriefing on execution and findings.\n  [3] (51) It is a recorded announcement for external parties.\n\n### ch3-q09 lens=[50,51,62,53] ca=2\nQ: What does the balanced delivery approach recommend for opening the exit interview?\n  [0] (50) Open with the most critical vulnerabilities first.\n  [1] (51) Start with unresolved fieldwork questions and gaps.\n  [2] (62) CORRECT* Begin with effective controls before covering vulnerabilities.\n  [3] (53) Present the reported risks in reverse severity order.\n\n### ch4-q07 lens=[57,46,47,46] ca=0\nQ: According to the reviewer, what may a cybersecurity expert identify during an expert interview?\n  [0] (57) CORRECT* security vulnerabilities the project team might overlook.\n  [1] (46) the exact budget needed for each work package.\n  [2] (47) the full list of tasks inside the project plan.\n  [3] (46) the delays caused by the documentation review.\n\n### ch4-q10 lens=[68,57,57,49] ca=0\nQ: Which of the following best describes the risk register and its role?\n  [0] (68) CORRECT* a document that records the risks identified throughout the project.\n  [1] (57) a tool that translates every threat into a dollar amount.\n  [2] (57) a chart that compares the current project with past ones.\n  [3] (49) a list that assigns owners to every work package.\n\n","metadata":{"output":"### ch1-q10 lens=[72,70,81,67] ca=2\nQ: Management wants to add background on why a server outage delayed a control test during the audit. Which exit interview purpose allows management to provide this explanation?\n  [0] (72) Clarify, so the auditor can verify the evidence used in the conclusions.\n  [1] (70) Discuss improvements, so the team can set corrective action deadlines.\n  [2] (81) CORRECT* Obtain the management response, which allows explanations and additional context.\n  [3] (67) Prepare, so the client c